All three site videos now resolve through videoAssets in lib/cdn.ts
rather than hardcoded public/ paths: the education demo on the use-case
page, the government demo, and the rehab clip in the human-delivery
section.

scripts/migrate-videos-to-r2.sh performs the one-time upload of the
existing files to stable videos/* keys and verifies each public URL,
including byte-range support so seeking works.

The local MP4s stay in place for now — per the rollback plan they are
removed only after CDN playback is verified in production.

